2.sw/README.md:261:1. When the CPU needs to update the routing table, it asserts the PAUSE signal by writing to the FCR register (i.e. `csr.dpe.fcr.pause = 1`).
2.sw/README.md:262:2. The active `csr.dpe.fcr.pause` signal instructs the input multiplexer to transition into the PAUSED state after completing the servicing of the current queue. The CPU periodically checks the ready bits in the FCR register.
2.sw/README.md:264:4. The processing of remaining packets and datapath clearing continues until all components transition to the IDLE state. The CPU monitors the ready bits in the FCR register, which now indicates that the DPE has been successfully paused (i.e. `csr.dpe.fcr.idle == 1`).
2.sw/README.md:266:6. Upon completing the updates, the CPU deactivates the PAUSE signal (i.e. `csr.dpe.fcr.pause = 0`).
